.TH TACA 1 "October 2026" "SDE" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
taca \- archive manager of the Selviana Desktop Environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B taca
[\fIFILE\fR...]
.br
.B taca
\fB\-\-extract\-here\fR \fIARCHIVE\fR...
.br
.B taca
\fB\-\-extract\-to\fR=\fIDIR\fR \fIARCHIVE\fR...
.br
.B taca
\fB\-\-add\-to\fR=\fIARCHIVE\fR \fIFILE\fR...
.br
.B taca
\fB\-\-list\fR | \fB\-\-test\fR \fIARCHIVE\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Taca opens, creates, changes and extracts archives. It is written for SDE
by the Selviana DE Project with SDE-FLTK and libarchive.
.PP
Without options, an archive \fIFILE\fR is opened in the Taca window and a
folder is browsed; other files are offered for packing into a new archive.
.SH WINDOW
The window has a menu bar (File, Commands, Tools, Favorites, Options and
Help), a toolbar, an address bar with an Up button, a details list and a
status bar with the totals of the folder and of the selection.
.PP
The list browses the file system: double-click a folder to open it, an
archive to look inside it (with its packed sizes and compression ratio) and
".." or Backspace to go up, out of the archive into its folder. Type a path
into the address bar (Ctrl+L), also a folder inside an archive such as
\fI~/Downloads/photos.zip/2026\fR.
.PP
The toolbar buttons:
.TP
.B Add
packs the selected files into a new archive, or adds files to the open one.
.TP
.B Extract To
extracts the open archive (or the selection inside it, or the selected
archives) into a folder, with options for existing files and folders.
.TP
.B Test
reads every member and checks it for errors.
.TP
.B View
shows a text file inside Taca or opens other files with their default
application.
.TP
.B Delete
removes members from the archive, or moves files to the trash.
.TP
.B Find
finds files by name patterns such as \fI*.txt;*.md\fR in the folder, its
sub-folders and, optionally, inside the archives found there.
.TP
.B Wizard
guides through creating, extracting or converting an archive.
.TP
.B Info
shows the format, sizes, ratio, encryption and comment of an archive.
.TP
.B Repair
saves the readable files of a damaged archive into a new one: with
\fBzip -FF\fR for ZIP files, \fBrar r\fR for RAR archives (both when
installed), 7-Zip or unrar for others, and otherwise libarchive, which
copies every member it can still read. The damaged archive is never changed.
.PP
Archive work runs in the background and can be cancelled. Files can be
dropped onto the window (to open an archive, pack files or add them to the
open archive) and dragged out of it to extract them.
.PP
Favorites keeps folders and archives you open often. Options sets the
default format and compression level, the view (details or icons), hidden
files and whether Taca follows the SDE theme or is always light or dark.
.SH KEYS
Alt+A add, Alt+E extract to, Alt+W extract here, Alt+T test, Alt+V view,
Alt+I information, Alt+R repair, Alt+Z wizard, Alt+Q convert, Del delete,
F2 rename, Enter open, Backspace up, F3 or Ctrl+F find, F5 refresh, Ctrl+B
add to favorites, Ctrl+H hidden files, Ctrl+O open, Ctrl+N new archive,
Ctrl+W close the archive, Ctrl+Q quit, F1 the list of keys.
.SH FORMATS
Read with libarchive: ZIP (and JAR, WAR, APK, EPUB, CBZ and other ZIP based
files), RAR 4 and RAR 5, 7z, tar, tar.gz, tar.bz2, tar.xz, tar.zst, tar.lz4,
tar.lzma, tar.lz, tar.Z, gz, bz2, xz, zst, lz4, lzma, lz, Z, ISO 9660, CAB,
cpio, ar, Debian packages, RPM, XAR, LHA and WARC.
.PP
Created with libarchive: ZIP (also with AES-256 passwords), 7z, tar,
tar.gz, tar.bz2, tar.xz, tar.zst, tar.lz4, ISO 9660, cpio, XAR and single
compressed files (gz, bz2, xz, zst, lz4, lzma, lz).
.PP
External programs are used when they are installed:
.BR 7z (1)
(package 7zip) for encrypted 7z archives (also with encrypted file names),
split volumes and AES ZIP archives when libarchive has no crypto support;
.BR unrar (1)
or 7-Zip for encrypted RAR archives; and
.BR rar (1)
to create or change RAR archives. Taca tells which package to install when
one is needed.
.SH SAFETY
Archives are untrusted. Members with absolute paths, ".." components,
drive letters or backslash traversal, symbolic links that point outside the
destination, members below such links, hard links to members that were not
extracted and device files are never written; Taca lists what it skipped.
Set-user-ID, set-group-ID and sticky bits are not restored. External tools
extract into a private folder first and Taca moves the result after the
same checks.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-extract\-here " " \fIARCHIVE\fR...
Extracts next to each archive. An archive with a single top-level item that
does not exist yet is extracted directly; otherwise a new folder named
after the archive is created.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-extract\-to =\fIDIR\fR " " \fIARCHIVE\fR...
Extracts into \fIDIR\fR (asks before creating it, see \fB\-\-force\fR).
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-extract " " \fIARCHIVE\fR...
Asks where and how to extract.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-add\-to =\fIARCHIVE\fR " " \fIFILE\fR...
Adds files to \fIARCHIVE\fR, creating it (format from its extension, ZIP
otherwise) when it does not exist.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-add " " \fIFILE\fR...
Asks for the name, format, compression level, password and volume size of
a new archive holding \fIFILE\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-default\-dir =\fIDIR\fR
Default folder for \fB\-\-extract\fR.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Creates the destination folder without asking.
.TP
.BR \-\-list " " \fIARCHIVE\fR
Prints the contents, one member per line, without a window.
.TP
.BR \-\-test " " \fIARCHIVE\fR
Reads every member and checks it, without a window.
.TP
.B \-\-formats
Prints what each format supports on this computer.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Prints the version.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Shows the options.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TACA_PASSWORD
Password used by \fB\-\-list\fR and \fB\-\-test\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/sde/taca-recent
Recently opened archives.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/sde/taca/
Temporary copies of opened and dragged files (removed after a day).
.TP
.I ~/.config/sde/sde.conf
Section [taca]: view=list|icons.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on errors, 2 for wrong usage, 3 when cancelled and 4 when
a password is needed or wrong (\fB\-\-list\fR, \fB\-\-test\fR).
